+/* Some file systems do not store every permission bit a caller requests.
+ * HarmonyOS HMDFS, for example, normalizes every mode without the owner
+ * execute bit to 0640, so a file created with 0660 or 0444 is stored as
+ * 0640.  Comparing all nine permission bits would therefore only ever pass
+ * on the file system the test was written for.  The checks below keep the
+ * upstream mode as the documented intent and pass a mask that restricts
+ * the comparison to the bits every target file system represents the same
+ * way, so a change to those bits still fails the test. */
 
 int verbose = 0;
 
